  "selection_rule": "Candidate dates are the union of the fourteen-date retention windows ending at each preserved wrapper's creation date, restricted to dates on or after 2026-09-06, when corpus schema v7 landed (older members are skipped by the restore as obsolete). The sample is the 28 most recent candidate dates, consecutive, so the primary 28-day frame is two retention windows as the plan sizes it. The runner restores each date from the preserved wrappers with --newest set to that date. Days with several daily runs (2026-10-02, 2026-10-06, 2026-10-08) have several wrappers, each archiving a fresh fetch of that day, and the restore fails closed when two wrappers disagree about a date; the runner therefore keeps only the newest wrapper per creation day (the run whose corpus the published briefing used and later wrappers carry forward) and lists the superseded wrappers in its merged manifest. Within the kept set, a date is supplied by every wrapper whose window contains it and any remaining conflict still fails closed.",
